WEBVTT

00:41.333 --> 00:43.961
NO TAIL TO TELL

00:47.172 --> 00:49.466
Fortunately, you have no major injuries.

00:50.384 --> 00:52.386
It's just some minor bruising.

00:54.805 --> 00:56.807
- This way!
- Okay.

00:56.890 --> 00:59.851
If this had landed just a bit off,

00:59.935 --> 01:01.562
it could've been much worse.

01:01.645 --> 01:03.188
You really were quite lucky.

01:08.527 --> 01:10.904
Maybe it's because
you were doing a good deed.

01:12.197 --> 01:14.241
I guess Heaven was watching over you.

01:14.324 --> 01:16.201
Right, yes.

01:16.285 --> 01:17.327
But…

01:18.829 --> 01:21.081
they say the universe has no compassion.

01:21.164 --> 01:25.711
You never know
if you'll be this lucky again.

01:27.713 --> 01:28.714
Pardon?

01:28.797 --> 01:32.301
I'm just saying you should be careful.

01:33.594 --> 01:34.636
I see.

01:38.599 --> 01:39.808
Thank you.

01:44.271 --> 01:45.355
Doctor?

01:46.732 --> 01:47.733
What…

01:50.902 --> 01:52.446
What are you doing? My gosh!

01:52.529 --> 01:54.740
I thought you were in here.

01:55.365 --> 01:57.534
No, I'm just coming back from outside.

01:57.618 --> 02:00.662
What? But that man just finished
a checkup with you.

02:00.746 --> 02:02.748
- Si-yeol!
- Where are you going?

02:02.831 --> 02:04.041
Si-yeol!

02:06.877 --> 02:08.170
Si-yeol!

02:11.089 --> 02:13.592
Where is Si-yeol?

02:16.136 --> 02:17.596
You looking for me?

02:20.849 --> 02:22.517
People will think I'm actually dead.

02:23.185 --> 02:25.479
Why are you calling out for me like that?
I'm right here.

02:25.562 --> 02:28.106
I seriously thought you were dead.

02:28.607 --> 02:30.025
Were you scared?

02:33.403 --> 02:34.321
Eun-ho.

02:35.238 --> 02:37.407
You told me to worry.

02:37.491 --> 02:40.035
You said I should worry about you!

02:40.911 --> 02:43.455
I'm really okay, I swear.

02:44.122 --> 02:47.125
Since when do you actually
listen to what I say?

02:57.761 --> 03:01.473
If you had died,
I would've killed you myself!

03:05.394 --> 03:08.188
You take worrying to a whole new level.

03:09.439 --> 03:11.483
Are you okay? Did you get hurt?

03:12.776 --> 03:15.612
They said I was lucky.
Just a small scratch here.

03:16.905 --> 03:18.365
You really scared me.

03:18.448 --> 03:21.201
You should've been right there
with me when I woke up.

03:21.284 --> 03:24.121
Man, that really hurts.

03:24.830 --> 03:25.997
Where were you?

03:26.623 --> 03:29.042
I was getting the test results.

03:29.126 --> 03:30.460
We're both perfectly fine.

03:31.461 --> 03:33.922
Really? That's a relief.

03:36.967 --> 03:38.301
Let's go.

03:39.928 --> 03:40.804
Where to?

03:40.887 --> 03:43.515
Where do you think? Home.

03:52.566 --> 03:55.819
EPISODE 7
THE REVENGE OF MEMORY

04:09.374 --> 04:13.170
What's with the mood?

04:13.253 --> 04:16.882
This is so awkward. Why is he so quiet?

04:46.578 --> 04:49.039
Oh… it's just that

04:50.207 --> 04:52.959
you had a leaf on your head.

04:53.043 --> 04:54.294
I see.

04:54.795 --> 04:56.171
Okay.

04:59.299 --> 05:01.927
What the hell? What's wrong with me?

05:02.010 --> 05:04.179
Why am I so self-conscious?

05:04.262 --> 05:07.057
He's just a human kid,
still wet behind the ears.

05:19.736 --> 05:21.780
Did you always look like this?

05:24.699 --> 05:25.700
What?

05:42.968 --> 05:45.595
Watch where you're going.

05:50.934 --> 05:53.103
What… was that for?

05:53.770 --> 05:56.273
- There was this bike behind you--
- Si-yeol!

05:57.732 --> 05:58.733
You.

05:59.943 --> 06:01.736
Don't walk so close to me anymore.

06:02.362 --> 06:05.323
- Why?
- Because…

06:09.661 --> 06:11.663
Do I really have to spell it out?

06:13.707 --> 06:15.000
Yes.

06:15.083 --> 06:16.251
Well…

06:18.128 --> 06:20.463
That's because…

06:20.547 --> 06:22.090
Hey, check them out.

06:28.179 --> 06:32.642
See? We're getting all these looks
because of you.

06:33.852 --> 06:36.479
Are you saying that's because of me?

06:36.563 --> 06:37.564
Of course.

06:38.273 --> 06:42.652
I feel bad that you ended up
looking like that after saving me,

06:42.736 --> 06:46.239
but you literally look like a beggar,
minus the tin cup.

06:46.865 --> 06:48.033
A beggar?

06:48.575 --> 06:50.368
Hey, I almost died back there!

06:50.452 --> 06:53.163
I'm saying that's how bad
you look right now,

06:53.246 --> 06:55.999
so don't walk so close to me.

06:57.667 --> 06:59.669
That's not going to make any difference.

07:00.420 --> 07:01.421
What?

07:01.504 --> 07:06.509
I'm saying you don't look
any better than I do.

07:06.593 --> 07:09.846
Are you saying I look like that too?

07:09.930 --> 07:12.974
I wasn't the only one in there.
Obviously, you look just as bad as I do.

07:13.058 --> 07:14.976
Oh no.

07:15.060 --> 07:16.645
I barely have any clothes as it is.

07:17.604 --> 07:20.649
I can't exactly walk around downtown
in hiking gear either.

07:21.942 --> 07:23.526
Given how things are,

07:24.069 --> 07:26.613
let's go buy some clothes
before we head home.

07:26.696 --> 07:28.323
- Really?
- Sure.

07:28.406 --> 07:30.617
We don't know
how long we'll be stuck like this,

07:30.700 --> 07:32.285
so you're going to need some clothes.

07:32.369 --> 07:33.453
Right.

07:33.536 --> 07:35.664
I was actually thinking about it anyway.

07:35.747 --> 07:37.123
Then,

07:37.707 --> 07:40.752
can I grab a few other things
while we're there?

07:42.087 --> 07:44.965
- Yeah, sure.
- Great, let's go!

07:59.938 --> 08:01.856
Do you even know
how much all this would cost?

08:01.940 --> 08:03.733
We got your wallet back.

08:03.817 --> 08:05.694
Yeah, but still.

08:05.777 --> 08:08.321
I'm not even sure
about my financial situation.

08:08.822 --> 08:11.199
You said you were buying.
Why are you backing out now?

08:11.282 --> 08:14.369
I meant a few basic T-shirts
and some jeans.

08:14.452 --> 08:17.539
- Not all this high-end stuff--
- Once we're back, we'll both be rich.

08:17.622 --> 08:20.417
Don't be cheap. Just swipe the card.

08:21.418 --> 08:22.460
But…

08:29.342 --> 08:33.346
This feels more like it.
Why was I acting so weird?

08:35.557 --> 08:37.642
He's just the same old Si-yeol.

08:58.538 --> 09:01.541
Silk pajamas? At a time like this?

09:01.624 --> 09:04.210
Just get a tracksuit
you can wear to the store

09:04.294 --> 09:06.171
and around the house.

09:06.671 --> 09:08.757
Don't you know
the importance of sleep quality?

09:08.840 --> 09:11.009
What if I'm too tired
to do anything right?

09:12.552 --> 09:14.179
Don't you want your life back?

09:16.222 --> 09:19.809
You're right.
Sleep quality is very important.

09:27.400 --> 09:29.402
Can't you just use cheap cucumber soap?

09:29.486 --> 09:30.653
That smells good too.

09:31.488 --> 09:33.281
- What?
- Nothing.

09:33.948 --> 09:35.742
Why am I even bothering?

09:35.825 --> 09:38.578
You bought bath bombs
when we don't even own a tub.

09:38.661 --> 09:41.664
Fine, buy all you want.

09:41.748 --> 09:42.624
There!

09:45.418 --> 09:48.505
- A phone?
- It's a pain not having one.

09:48.588 --> 09:50.632
Mine's still stuck
at Myohyangsan Mountain.

09:50.715 --> 09:53.551
You don't even have anyone to call.

09:55.553 --> 09:57.597
I'm going to be calling you.

10:01.434 --> 10:03.144
Perfect. Let's get this one.

10:03.937 --> 10:06.648
What? You want to buy this?

10:06.731 --> 10:09.651
Why do we need
such a giant TV for that tiny house?

10:09.734 --> 10:12.112
I can't stand small screens.

10:12.195 --> 10:15.323
Haven't you heard?
The bigger the TV, the better.

10:16.407 --> 10:19.202
How can a nine-tailed fox
be so materialistic?

10:19.285 --> 10:22.831
Like you said, who knows
how long we'll be stuck like this?

10:22.914 --> 10:24.040
Just swipe the card.

10:33.800 --> 10:36.970
Excuse me, sir.
It says you have insufficient funds.

10:37.053 --> 10:40.306
See? I told you we're broke.

10:40.849 --> 10:43.226
Let's just get a refund for everything.

10:44.018 --> 10:45.687
Hey. Wait!

10:46.896 --> 10:48.273
Damn it.

10:50.608 --> 10:53.403
Hey, are you crazy?

10:53.486 --> 10:54.487
Unbelievable.

10:59.617 --> 11:01.828
What? Did you say something?

11:03.454 --> 11:06.958
Oh no. Look at that. The tag fell off.

11:09.419 --> 11:10.378
Hello.

11:10.461 --> 11:11.880
HYEON WOO-SEOK SIGNING EVENT
ONE MILLION COPIES SOLD

11:13.047 --> 11:14.966
Thank you. You're so handsome.

11:15.049 --> 11:16.759
- Can I get a photo?
- Sure.

11:18.511 --> 11:20.430
- You're so cool.
- One second, please.

11:20.513 --> 11:22.390
This is for you.

11:24.976 --> 11:26.102
Thank you.

11:28.563 --> 11:30.064
- Good luck!
- Thanks.

11:31.816 --> 11:34.152
Hi. What's your name?

11:42.160 --> 11:45.038
What's this? Why do you carry
something like this around?

11:47.790 --> 11:48.875
Lee Yoon.

11:51.711 --> 11:53.504
My given name is one syllable.

11:53.588 --> 11:56.257
Last name Lee, first name Yoon.

11:58.927 --> 12:01.054
My given name is one syllable.

12:01.763 --> 12:03.056
Last name Lee,

12:04.557 --> 12:05.683
first name Yoon.

12:14.651 --> 12:15.818
You.

12:19.364 --> 12:21.991
So, you remember me?

12:22.617 --> 12:24.786
That was so long ago.
You must have a good memory.

12:24.869 --> 12:26.204
You bastard!

12:27.288 --> 12:29.290
Hey, Woo-seok. Woo-seok!

12:29.374 --> 12:31.000
Whoa… hey!

12:33.211 --> 12:34.671
- Damn it!
- Oh my gosh!

12:35.797 --> 12:37.715
That hurts!

12:44.264 --> 12:46.182
This is more like it.

12:46.266 --> 12:48.810
- Unbelievable.
- Home sweet home.

12:48.893 --> 12:50.979
If you can even call this a home.

12:51.688 --> 12:53.523
How did I get stuck with someone like her?

12:54.357 --> 12:56.901
I only bought the essentials.

12:56.985 --> 13:01.322
Seriously, what are we going to do
now that we're out of money?

13:01.406 --> 13:02.949
Do you even have a plan?

13:04.659 --> 13:06.286
We can always make more money.

13:06.369 --> 13:08.579
- Who? You?
- Yes, me.

13:08.663 --> 13:11.833
All you know is soccer.
Do you have any other skills?

13:12.583 --> 13:13.668
Are you serious?

13:13.751 --> 13:17.880
I've lived for centuries.
Do you think I've wasted that time?

13:17.964 --> 13:20.633
I've got plenty of skills.

13:20.717 --> 13:23.886
I'm good at everything I do,
so don't you worry.

13:24.512 --> 13:26.806
Can I really count on you?

13:26.889 --> 13:28.016
Of course.

13:28.099 --> 13:30.852
Ever heard of the term "hobby-rich"?

13:30.935 --> 13:33.938
I've tried every single thing
that looked even remotely fun.

13:34.731 --> 13:37.775
You probably didn't know,
but I even speak English.

13:38.401 --> 13:39.736
Wait, you speak English?

13:39.819 --> 13:42.155
I graduated from Yejeong Academy.

13:42.697 --> 13:43.698
And that's not all.

13:43.781 --> 13:47.410
From woodworking and coffee making
to baking and knitting,

13:47.493 --> 13:48.995
I've learned it all.

13:49.746 --> 13:52.123
Supporting you would be a piece of cake.

13:53.499 --> 13:55.460
I really want to believe you.

13:56.794 --> 13:59.005
But I can't for some reason.

14:03.009 --> 14:07.388
Anyway, even if your fate has changed,
why are you so broke?

14:08.097 --> 14:11.559
It's insane that one shopping trip
emptied your entire account.

14:13.519 --> 14:14.937
Yeah, you're right about that.

14:15.563 --> 14:18.775
I may only be in the fourth division,
but I've still been earning for a while.

14:18.858 --> 14:22.862
It's not like I have a car
or even a nice house.

14:24.364 --> 14:26.991
Do I have a separate
savings account somewhere?

14:27.075 --> 14:28.368
I should look into it.

14:28.451 --> 14:33.039
Trust me, squeeze someone hard enough,
and they'll come up with the money.

14:33.122 --> 14:34.207
There's always a way out.

14:36.167 --> 14:38.127
I should just stop talking to you.

14:39.170 --> 14:42.006
Anyway, tell me
what the plan is from here.

14:42.090 --> 14:43.091
What?

14:43.174 --> 14:47.303
Don't tell me you're going to pull
that false kindness stunt again.

14:47.929 --> 14:50.014
What happened this time
was just a total coincidence,

14:50.098 --> 14:51.474
so we got to save those kids.

14:51.557 --> 14:54.060
But we can't rely on flukes like that.

14:55.269 --> 14:58.398
It wasn't a coincidence. It was fate.

14:59.565 --> 15:02.693
I guess the ones above
actually have a conscience.

15:02.777 --> 15:05.154
Seeing how they're finally
cooperating with us.

15:06.697 --> 15:08.408
What are you talking about?

15:08.491 --> 15:11.244
I'm saying everything is going well,
so stop worrying.

15:13.287 --> 15:15.373
How many young lives
did we save today?

15:15.456 --> 15:17.375
It had to be at least ten, right?

15:17.458 --> 15:19.377
Yeah, I guess so.

15:20.002 --> 15:23.506
The merit of saving just one life
is beyond measure.

15:24.173 --> 15:27.677
But saving that many children
with their whole lives ahead of them

15:27.760 --> 15:30.054
on the very first day
we started doing good deeds?

15:30.972 --> 15:33.766
It means Heaven is determined to help us.

15:34.475 --> 15:35.351
You think so?

15:35.435 --> 15:37.061
I'm sure of it.

15:37.145 --> 15:40.148
We must have gained
decades' worth of spiritual power today.

15:40.898 --> 15:44.068
I bet she got the shock of her life
while she was eating her greens

15:44.152 --> 15:45.862
up on the mountain.

15:45.945 --> 15:47.405
I don't think so.

15:47.488 --> 15:48.781
- You scared me!
- Jeez!

15:49.866 --> 15:52.201
- When did you get here?
- Just now.

15:54.454 --> 15:58.207
It's different when it happens to me.
I'll never get used to this.

16:00.209 --> 16:03.171
Next time, knock before you come in.

16:03.254 --> 16:06.048
Don't just pop up out of nowhere, okay?

16:06.132 --> 16:08.217
- Okay.
- Wait.

16:08.301 --> 16:11.262
What do you mean, you don't think so?

16:11.345 --> 16:14.682
Right, I just don't think things
are going very well right now.

16:14.765 --> 16:17.185
And I don't think Heaven
is helping you at all.

16:18.144 --> 16:19.187
What?

16:28.529 --> 16:31.616
We haven't gained
one bit of spiritual power.

16:32.408 --> 16:34.744
That makes no sense.
Are you sure about that?

16:38.998 --> 16:40.750
It's exactly the same as yesterday.

16:41.250 --> 16:43.753
Are you sure you're doing this right?

16:43.836 --> 16:46.964
Why? What's the problem?

16:48.299 --> 16:51.427
I don't know what's going on.

16:51.511 --> 16:52.512
What?

16:53.137 --> 16:54.931
Something's not right.

16:55.014 --> 16:57.683
I don't know why,
but this shouldn't be happening.

16:59.769 --> 17:03.272
What do we do now, Si-yeol?

17:12.448 --> 17:13.950
Man, I can taste blood.

17:17.161 --> 17:18.204
Here.

17:19.830 --> 17:22.792
Are you okay?
Maybe you should go to the hospital.

17:22.875 --> 17:24.252
I'm fine.

17:26.462 --> 17:30.132
Hey, apologize to him right now
before things get worse.

17:31.259 --> 17:34.095
Apologize?
Dad, don't you remember this guy?

17:34.178 --> 17:36.639
Don't you remember
what happened to my life because…

17:39.517 --> 17:41.477
What about your life?

17:44.647 --> 17:46.357
Do you two know each other?

17:48.276 --> 17:51.946
Well, you could say that.

17:53.739 --> 17:57.702
It seems we're more
deeply entangled than I thought.

17:58.452 --> 18:01.455
Seeing how you reacted
to that business card earlier.

18:01.539 --> 18:03.332
I think we should talk in private.

18:04.584 --> 18:06.377
Could you give us a moment?

18:07.336 --> 18:09.672
I really should--

18:09.755 --> 18:11.173
Dad.

18:11.257 --> 18:13.050
Just step outside for a minute.

18:31.902 --> 18:33.154
Jeez.

18:33.237 --> 18:35.323
If looks could kill, man.

18:37.158 --> 18:39.744
You've seen this before, haven't you?

18:41.454 --> 18:42.455
This right here.

18:45.875 --> 18:48.961
Your face tells me everything.

18:50.087 --> 18:55.176
But this is just a fake I whipped up.

18:56.677 --> 18:58.596
I was just curious to see your reaction.

19:05.478 --> 19:06.812
What are you trying to say?

19:06.896 --> 19:07.938
Just that…

19:09.357 --> 19:11.067
if you're a client
of that nine-tailed fox,

19:11.150 --> 19:12.568
I have a favor to ask.

19:14.153 --> 19:15.071
A favor?

19:16.155 --> 19:21.661
You see, I've had
a bit of a misunderstanding with her.

19:22.495 --> 19:25.956
I can't keep avoiding her forever,
so I want to talk things out.

19:26.582 --> 19:29.669
I'd like you to act
as a messenger between us.

19:30.419 --> 19:33.214
Of course, I'll make it worth your while.

19:38.803 --> 19:40.221
Why on earth would I do that?

19:40.304 --> 19:44.058
I want to see your life ruined
more than anyone.

19:44.767 --> 19:46.143
Kang Si-yeol.

19:46.811 --> 19:48.813
He must be a very close friend of yours.

19:50.064 --> 19:51.107
I mean, think about it.

19:51.190 --> 19:54.860
I didn't hit you,
and I didn't ruin your life.

19:54.944 --> 19:59.448
And you're still getting this emotional.
Don't you think that's a bit much?

20:00.116 --> 20:01.992
Watch your damn mouth.

20:02.076 --> 20:04.412
You weren't actually doing this for me.

20:05.830 --> 20:06.914
You just couldn't go back?

20:10.876 --> 20:13.546
- Are you afraid I might get in the way?
- You tell me.

20:13.629 --> 20:15.214
I think you're fully capable of that.

20:16.674 --> 20:18.634
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

20:23.055 --> 20:24.515
What are you doing?

20:24.598 --> 20:25.808
This memory…

20:26.475 --> 20:28.227
I found a way!

20:28.310 --> 20:29.729
I don't think it's mine.

20:30.271 --> 20:31.564
Why does this keep happening?

20:32.773 --> 20:35.025
What memory?

20:36.610 --> 20:37.778
You just couldn't go back?

20:39.321 --> 20:41.115
Couldn't go back to what?

20:41.198 --> 20:43.367
Are you afraid I might get in the way?

20:44.118 --> 20:46.245
I might get in the way of something?

20:47.663 --> 20:50.666
Did the nine-tailed fox
mess with your memories?

20:52.752 --> 20:53.836
Erase it.

20:53.919 --> 20:55.171
No, wait--

20:57.089 --> 20:58.132
I think so.

20:58.924 --> 21:00.217
Why?

21:00.301 --> 21:02.553
You're the client,
and she erased your memory?

21:09.101 --> 21:10.478
I don't know.

21:12.438 --> 21:16.358
I think I found something out,
and she thought I'd get in the way.

21:16.984 --> 21:19.570
You found something out?

21:22.823 --> 21:24.742
You mean like a weakness?

21:24.825 --> 21:26.243
I don't know. I can't remember!

21:26.327 --> 21:27.828
Okay, I get it. Calm down.

21:27.912 --> 21:30.122
Then, if I help you recover
those memories,

21:30.206 --> 21:33.167
will you tell me
what it was you found out?

21:37.046 --> 21:41.884
I happen to know someone
who can help with this.

21:43.928 --> 21:45.471
I'm really curious.

21:46.013 --> 21:49.809
What did you find out that she had to

21:50.476 --> 21:52.269
go as far as erasing your memories?

22:06.116 --> 22:09.787
What if I stay human
and just die of old age?

22:11.205 --> 22:12.832
Why isn't the power building up?

22:17.002 --> 22:19.505
I've been thinking.

22:19.588 --> 22:20.714
Yeah?

22:21.423 --> 22:23.175
Maybe…

22:24.969 --> 22:26.679
…the problem is your attitude.

22:28.472 --> 22:29.557
What?

22:29.640 --> 22:31.600
Think about it.

22:32.142 --> 22:33.561
Going by what you said,

22:33.644 --> 22:36.689
you must do good deeds
to gain spiritual power.

22:36.772 --> 22:39.900
But you tried to wait for someone to jump
so you could save them.

22:39.984 --> 22:41.402
You also tried to start a fire.

22:41.485 --> 22:45.781
That kind of thinking shouldn't be
the basis for doing good deeds.

22:48.492 --> 22:55.124
You're starting to sound
just as picky and petty as the ones above,

22:55.207 --> 22:57.626
but this is different.

22:57.710 --> 23:00.421
We saved children
who were in actual danger.

23:00.504 --> 23:02.464
Well, in hindsight, sure.

23:02.548 --> 23:05.593
But I'm saying your mindset
was wrong from the start.

23:05.676 --> 23:07.970
So what's your point?

23:12.057 --> 23:13.475
For starters,

23:14.184 --> 23:17.313
how about we try
doing good deeds by the book?

23:18.647 --> 23:20.190
Do you know how long that will take?

23:20.274 --> 23:22.526
It could take a hundred,
even two hundred years.

23:23.235 --> 23:26.697
Yet you expect me to waste my time
picking up trash in some neighborhood?

23:26.780 --> 23:28.365
That's not what I meant,

23:28.866 --> 23:31.160
but we need to find out for sure

23:31.785 --> 23:34.705
whether doing good deeds
actually builds spiritual power or not

23:34.788 --> 23:38.000
and if you can really
build up that power for her.

23:38.083 --> 23:39.335
Once we confirm that,

23:39.418 --> 23:42.046
then we can find another way,
be it fake or not.

23:42.129 --> 23:44.131
Doesn't that make sense to you?

23:44.965 --> 23:46.258
I guess.

23:46.842 --> 23:49.178
Something undeniable.

23:49.261 --> 23:53.933
Something we can do
sincerely without cutting corners.

23:54.016 --> 23:55.809
You know, that kind of good deed.

23:56.435 --> 23:58.228
Like volunteer work, for example.

23:59.688 --> 24:01.231
Volunteer work?

24:03.651 --> 24:05.402
What would be good?

24:08.572 --> 24:10.866
Right, something like that.

24:16.177 --> 24:21.043
FOREVER CARE NURSING HOME

24:24.380 --> 24:26.966
Are you here to do some volunteer work?

24:27.841 --> 24:30.260
What, do you think I'm here
to be looked after?

24:30.844 --> 24:32.429
There's that attitude again. Watch it!

24:34.431 --> 24:36.266
What kind of volunteer work are you--

24:36.350 --> 24:39.144
You know, the hard stuff.

24:39.228 --> 24:41.063
Ideally, something physical.

24:41.647 --> 24:43.440
Hi, it's been a while.

24:44.775 --> 24:46.860
I'm sorry, do I know you?

24:47.361 --> 24:49.405
Please come this way.

24:50.030 --> 24:51.615
Do you know her?

24:52.282 --> 24:54.201
No, I've never seen her before.

24:55.452 --> 24:57.037
Whatever, let's just go.

25:13.220 --> 25:17.307
It's just cloth, for crying out loud!
How is it so heavy?

25:18.225 --> 25:20.519
Because it's wet.

25:20.602 --> 25:21.979
I know that.

25:22.062 --> 25:24.231
Stop complaining
and put some effort into it.

25:24.314 --> 25:27.151
That's the only way
all this work will mean anything.

25:29.486 --> 25:30.529
Here.

25:31.488 --> 25:32.740
Hey, wait.

25:35.951 --> 25:38.829
So? Do you feel
the spiritual power building up?

25:39.413 --> 25:40.622
I don't know.

25:41.874 --> 25:46.211
What if I work myself to the bone
and leave empty-handed again?

25:46.295 --> 25:48.213
Let's just wait and see.

25:49.256 --> 25:51.967
Try to have a better attitude, okay?

25:52.051 --> 25:53.927
I'm trying.

25:55.429 --> 25:59.266
Why are these clothes so uncomfortable?

25:59.349 --> 26:02.728
For how expensive they are,
they're more trouble than they're worth.

26:04.021 --> 26:05.898
It's not the clothes' fault.

26:06.648 --> 26:09.276
Who wears something like that
to a place like this?

26:10.611 --> 26:13.572
It's because
I only have clothes like these.

26:15.824 --> 26:17.367
I have a lot to say about that,

26:17.451 --> 26:20.454
but it won't do any good,
so I'll just keep it to myself.

26:38.222 --> 26:42.559
Still, in this day and age,
at least we have these machines.

26:42.643 --> 26:46.271
You wouldn't know, but back in the day,

26:46.772 --> 26:50.901
we washed laundry at the creek
and dried it in the sun.

26:50.984 --> 26:52.361
That's how everyone lived.

26:53.028 --> 26:55.114
So many years lived,

26:55.197 --> 26:58.951
yet still so immature, Ms. Kim Ok-sun.

26:59.701 --> 27:00.744
What?

27:01.537 --> 27:02.746
Nothing.

27:02.830 --> 27:05.415
Anyway, you should appreciate
how easy life is now.

27:05.499 --> 27:08.502
If I had to wash and dry these
like the old days,

27:08.585 --> 27:11.213
there's no way
you could've made me do this.

27:17.177 --> 27:19.054
What's wrong all of a sudden?

27:36.738 --> 27:39.283
Talk about terrible timing.

27:39.366 --> 27:41.952
Why did the dryer have to break
today of all days,

27:42.035 --> 27:44.371
when I'm working here?

27:44.454 --> 27:46.707
Better than the washer breaking,
don't you think?

27:46.790 --> 27:48.417
Man, if that had happened,

27:48.500 --> 27:50.794
we'd be in one of those red tubs
like in some drama,

27:50.878 --> 27:53.046
stomping on blankets together.

27:56.758 --> 28:00.262
What, do you want to get in the tub
with me or something?

28:00.345 --> 28:01.346
What?

28:01.430 --> 28:04.725
I thought you were doing that again.
You know, flirting.

28:06.143 --> 28:09.479
Jeez, where do you learn
all this weird stuff?

28:09.563 --> 28:11.732
Stop describing everything as flirting.

28:11.815 --> 28:15.277
No need to be so serious.
Just help me shake out this blanket.

28:32.085 --> 28:35.047
How are those humans
still so into each other

28:35.130 --> 28:37.090
when they're already so old?

28:38.300 --> 28:40.594
They look happy together.

28:41.553 --> 28:44.514
What's it like?
That "dating" thing humans do.

28:45.933 --> 28:47.142
What?

28:47.226 --> 28:50.145
Don't tell me
you've never dated anyone either?

28:50.771 --> 28:52.773
Don't be ridiculous.

28:52.856 --> 28:55.901
I'm Kang Si-yeol.
Do you think that'd even be possible?

28:55.984 --> 28:58.445
I didn't ask who you were.

28:58.528 --> 29:00.447
What I'm wondering is

29:00.530 --> 29:04.201
how someone can love
another person for that long?

29:05.577 --> 29:07.788
No matter how great a human is,

29:08.455 --> 29:11.667
you can always find flaws.

29:11.750 --> 29:14.503
You're also bound to get tired
of each other eventually.

29:16.338 --> 29:17.798
I wouldn't know.

29:19.174 --> 29:22.427
I've never really dated anyone
for that long, actually.

29:22.511 --> 29:25.847
See? I told you humans get boring.

29:25.931 --> 29:27.266
No, that's not it.

29:31.478 --> 29:33.605
You might find this very hard to believe,

29:33.689 --> 29:37.526
but I'm always the one
who gets dumped.

29:39.069 --> 29:40.112
What?

29:40.612 --> 29:43.115
After all that bragging?

29:44.032 --> 29:45.117
Why?

29:45.200 --> 29:48.787
I don't know. It's always the same reason.

29:48.870 --> 29:51.832
They ask how I can
prioritize soccer over them.

29:51.915 --> 29:54.459
But what can I do?
I'm a professional athlete.

29:54.543 --> 29:56.086
Soccer has to come first.

29:56.712 --> 30:00.215
Oh, forget it.
I'm the idiot for even asking you.

30:13.353 --> 30:17.107
But you said you've done everything
in the human world.

30:17.983 --> 30:19.651
How come you've never dated?

30:20.694 --> 30:21.820
Because I knew a fox

30:21.903 --> 30:24.865
who totally ruined her life
by falling in love with a human.

30:27.909 --> 30:29.870
I made myself a promise after seeing that.

30:29.953 --> 30:32.789
I'll never love a human,

30:32.873 --> 30:34.791
and I'll never become one.

30:35.709 --> 30:38.003
I vowed to never live like her.

30:41.590 --> 30:44.384
Not that any of that matters.
Look at me now.

30:55.270 --> 30:56.146
Oh, that's cold.

30:57.022 --> 30:58.023
What was that for?

30:58.899 --> 31:00.192
Don't act like it's all over.

31:01.818 --> 31:03.653
I mean, the game isn't over yet.

31:03.737 --> 31:06.156
Even if you're down two goals
in the first half,

31:06.239 --> 31:09.034
you just have to score three
in the second half to win.

31:09.659 --> 31:11.536
We may be struggling right now,

31:11.620 --> 31:14.873
but we'll find a way
and get back to how we were.

31:17.584 --> 31:18.835
I never said we wouldn't.

31:20.295 --> 31:22.589
I'm just saying because you look so down.

31:23.423 --> 31:25.842
Come on.
Let's finish hanging these blankets.

31:37.062 --> 31:38.605
What was that for?

31:38.688 --> 31:41.817
I'm older than you.
Don't try to lecture me.

31:41.900 --> 31:44.194
I'm not lecturing you. Stop it!

31:44.277 --> 31:45.904
- Stop what?
- Stop!

31:45.987 --> 31:47.197
I'm serious!

31:49.366 --> 31:51.076
Hey, you're getting the blankets wet!

31:51.159 --> 31:52.744
So stay right there!

31:55.247 --> 31:56.415
Wait!

32:21.481 --> 32:23.942
Damn, what is…

32:24.985 --> 32:26.695
What's with this place?

32:27.320 --> 32:28.572
Is this really

32:29.489 --> 32:31.450
Jang Do-cheol's house?

32:32.075 --> 32:33.034
Yes, sir.

32:33.743 --> 32:36.580
How can anyone live in a place like this?

32:36.663 --> 32:37.873
This place is creepy.

32:39.499 --> 32:44.045
- Are you sure this is the right place?
- This is the last address on record, sir.

32:44.588 --> 32:47.007
He doesn't really leave any traces behind.

32:47.090 --> 32:49.176
What about his number?
Doesn't he have a phone?

32:50.385 --> 32:51.428
No, sir.

32:52.220 --> 32:56.600
Seriously, where the hell is he hiding?

32:57.225 --> 32:59.561
I finally found a lead, and now this.

33:04.483 --> 33:06.067
Hey, wait for me!

33:22.417 --> 33:24.669
Unbelievable.

33:26.046 --> 33:28.882
Does anyone
in the neighborhood know anything?

33:28.965 --> 33:30.759
Well, I asked around.

33:31.426 --> 33:33.553
Apparently, he moved here
about ten years ago

33:33.637 --> 33:36.223
and lived with his family for a while.

33:37.307 --> 33:38.934
Family?

33:39.601 --> 33:41.144
He had a family?

33:42.646 --> 33:46.399
Yes, but apparently
not long after they moved in,

33:46.483 --> 33:49.486
his wife and daughter both died.

33:49.569 --> 33:50.779
From what I heard,

33:51.947 --> 33:53.573
they met a horrific end.

33:57.661 --> 33:58.828
Really?

33:58.912 --> 34:00.914
According to the neighbors,

34:00.997 --> 34:03.542
his whole family was cursed

34:04.501 --> 34:08.672
because he tried to refuse
the shamanic calling.

34:09.214 --> 34:12.133
Anyway, they said
he's been a bit crazy ever since.

34:13.468 --> 34:16.638
What was that? What is it?

34:18.890 --> 34:22.519
Damn you. Seriously.

34:22.602 --> 34:24.354
Forget that crap.

34:24.437 --> 34:26.606
Just find out where that bastard is.

34:27.232 --> 34:28.775
I need him right now.

34:30.694 --> 34:32.988
- Let's get out of here.
- Mr. Lee.

34:33.905 --> 34:37.117
My goodness! What happened?

34:37.200 --> 34:38.994
I'm sorry.

34:39.077 --> 34:42.205
I told you to dry the laundry,
not soak it all over again.

34:42.872 --> 34:44.374
What am I supposed to do now?

34:45.083 --> 34:47.502
It's sunny out. It'll dry in no time.

34:48.169 --> 34:49.754
- Hey!
- What?

34:51.881 --> 34:54.009
Anyway, good job today.

34:54.092 --> 34:56.303
Go get something to eat. Unbelievable.

34:56.386 --> 34:59.472
Okay. I'm so sorry.

35:01.558 --> 35:04.269
Man, I told you to stop messing around.

35:04.352 --> 35:06.354
Who told you to hide behind the blankets?

35:06.438 --> 35:08.690
I didn't think
you'd spray water there too.

35:08.773 --> 35:11.359
Whatever. I'm starving, so let's go eat.

35:11.443 --> 35:13.612
Hold on a second.

35:30.086 --> 35:32.505
Have I gone crazy since becoming human?

35:35.842 --> 35:38.553
I thought I was fine.
Why is this happening again?

35:39.596 --> 35:43.058
What do you think you're doing?

35:43.141 --> 35:44.893
I can't go eat like this.

35:45.602 --> 35:48.438
There's too much water to just shake off.

36:16.508 --> 36:19.052
Wait, what's with my body?

36:19.135 --> 36:20.053
What?

36:20.637 --> 36:23.014
My body wasn't like this before.

36:24.265 --> 36:26.184
How badly did I take care of myself?

36:26.267 --> 36:28.144
Did I not work out properly?

36:28.770 --> 36:31.147
Why? It looks good.

36:33.233 --> 36:34.150
What?

36:34.234 --> 36:35.151
Nothing.

36:35.235 --> 36:38.863
Just put your shirt back on.
Have some decency.

36:38.947 --> 36:41.616
Wait. Let me just wring out the water.

36:41.700 --> 36:43.326
I said put it back on already!

36:43.410 --> 36:46.371
- What's wrong with you?
- Put it on!

37:00.510 --> 37:01.594
Si-yeol?

37:13.648 --> 37:16.359
What… was he doing?

37:16.443 --> 37:20.572
Me? I didn't do anything!

37:20.655 --> 37:22.407
Si-yeol, we're in a nursing home.

37:22.490 --> 37:24.826
Are you crazy?
There are old people everywhere!

37:24.909 --> 37:29.289
I know how this might look,
but it's not like that.

37:29.372 --> 37:31.791
See? I told you to put your shirt back on!

37:31.875 --> 37:34.502
How shameless could you be,
stripping down in public?

37:35.253 --> 37:38.089
Don't you guys get any ideas.
It's not like that!

37:52.353 --> 37:54.355
Hey, what are you guys looking at?

37:55.482 --> 37:57.984
Come on. Aren't you going to introduce us?

37:58.067 --> 38:00.111
What do you mean?

38:04.949 --> 38:06.493
Fine, whatever.

38:06.576 --> 38:07.619
She's my girlfriend.

38:08.745 --> 38:09.746
What?

38:11.956 --> 38:13.333
What?

38:13.416 --> 38:14.959
How else should I explain it to them?

38:15.043 --> 38:17.295
They barge into my house all the time.

38:17.378 --> 38:19.172
We live together, remember?

38:19.255 --> 38:21.299
- You live together?
- Since when?

38:21.382 --> 38:24.385
I guess it won't be for long anyway.

38:25.011 --> 38:26.888
Pardon? What does that mean?

38:26.971 --> 38:28.598
What won't be for long?

38:29.265 --> 38:30.850
Si-yeol, are you getting married?

38:33.144 --> 38:34.395
What?

38:34.479 --> 38:37.732
Please. Nobody's getting married.

38:40.485 --> 38:41.694
Are you?

38:43.029 --> 38:45.448
Sure, we're getting married too.

38:45.532 --> 38:47.909
That's taking it too far.

38:47.992 --> 38:49.911
That's too far?

38:50.537 --> 38:53.039
- Just eat your food.
- I didn't know.

38:53.122 --> 38:55.708
You jerk. I didn't know you had it in you!

38:55.792 --> 38:58.086
You're the worst, Si-yeol.

38:58.169 --> 39:00.672
Anyway, what are you guys doing here?

39:01.506 --> 39:03.508
What are you talking about?

39:03.591 --> 39:05.552
They're our team's main sponsor.

39:06.052 --> 39:08.888
You know we come here regularly.

39:08.972 --> 39:11.224
As part of our required community service.

39:12.267 --> 39:13.852
- I see.
- But today,

39:13.935 --> 39:16.896
they said someone already did
all the heavy lifting.

39:16.980 --> 39:18.606
So there's not much for us to do.

39:18.690 --> 39:20.733
It just worked out that way.

39:20.817 --> 39:24.696
Wait. Was it you
who did all the heavy lifting?

39:25.947 --> 39:27.991
You didn't come to see your grandma?

39:29.075 --> 39:30.994
Grandma? Which grandma?

39:32.287 --> 39:33.830
Your grandmother.

39:34.706 --> 39:35.915
Your own grandmother.

39:35.999 --> 39:37.208
What?

39:37.292 --> 39:38.960
My grandma who passed away?

39:45.884 --> 39:47.218
- What?
- Wait.

39:47.886 --> 39:49.554
Who passed away?

39:50.263 --> 39:51.139
My grandma.

39:52.307 --> 39:53.349
What?

39:54.559 --> 39:55.768
What?

40:00.440 --> 40:01.608
There!

40:02.567 --> 40:05.320
Now, what do we have here?

40:06.946 --> 40:08.323
There we go!

40:10.617 --> 40:13.786
Man, I'm on a roll!
The cards are just going my way.

40:13.870 --> 40:16.581
You're good at this, Coach.

40:17.457 --> 40:21.085
I came by to give you some pocket money
since it's been a while,

40:21.169 --> 40:23.254
but my luck just won't let me.

40:24.213 --> 40:25.757
Should I go easy on you?

40:25.840 --> 40:28.593
Now, that wouldn't be right.

40:28.676 --> 40:30.219
- There.
- Look at that!

40:32.847 --> 40:34.098
Let's see.

40:35.683 --> 40:37.644
Here.

40:39.103 --> 40:40.438
Gosh, I'm in trouble.

40:46.611 --> 40:48.863
- Oh my.
- You brat.

40:48.947 --> 40:50.865
Don't just stand there. Come on in.

40:52.784 --> 40:53.701
Grandma?

40:53.785 --> 40:55.912
Look who's here. My grandson.

41:07.131 --> 41:08.216
Go on.

41:25.984 --> 41:27.527
It really is my grandma.

41:29.445 --> 41:30.530
What's wrong?

41:32.323 --> 41:33.574
Did something happen?

41:35.284 --> 41:36.369
Tell me.

41:40.456 --> 41:41.624
Oh my.

41:54.137 --> 41:55.430
Grandma.

41:55.513 --> 41:56.806
There, there.

42:27.879 --> 42:30.506
I don't drink stuff like this.

42:31.049 --> 42:32.842
Just hold on to it then.

42:32.925 --> 42:35.178
I just didn't want to drink alone.

42:45.646 --> 42:48.107
What are you doing, scaring her like that?

42:49.275 --> 42:50.359
I just…

42:51.694 --> 42:52.612
It's just that--

42:52.695 --> 42:54.530
If it's about her nursing home bills…

42:57.533 --> 42:59.994
I kept your name
on the team roster for now.

43:00.745 --> 43:05.541
So the team sponsor's hospital discount

43:06.167 --> 43:09.128
should still be good for a while.

43:11.130 --> 43:12.799
Just so you know.

43:17.887 --> 43:21.641
Don't you dare get the wrong idea.

43:22.433 --> 43:25.478
It's not like I'm sitting around
waiting for you to come back.

43:25.561 --> 43:27.355
It's just because of your grandma.

43:27.438 --> 43:29.565
I'm only doing this for her sake.

43:30.817 --> 43:33.444
You're full of surprises.

43:35.404 --> 43:37.740
I thought you hated me

43:38.407 --> 43:39.826
ever since I was young.

43:39.909 --> 43:41.452
I do hate you, you punk.

43:41.536 --> 43:45.373
I haven't liked you since you were a kid,
not even a little,

43:46.165 --> 43:47.667
and nothing's changed.

43:50.253 --> 43:51.963
Guess we feel the same way then.

43:53.089 --> 43:55.258
Jeez, this little brat.

44:02.306 --> 44:04.851
This actually tastes good
after all this time.

44:16.112 --> 44:17.280
Grandma.

44:18.614 --> 44:21.409
Is it getting harder for you
to move around?

44:22.535 --> 44:24.871
That's just part of getting old.

44:25.621 --> 44:29.458
It's actually easier here
since they take care of everything for me.

44:31.085 --> 44:32.670
Nothing else is bothering you?

44:32.753 --> 44:34.547
No, I'm fine.

44:40.011 --> 44:43.723
Is something not working out
the way you wanted?

44:44.432 --> 44:45.725
What?

44:45.808 --> 44:49.270
It's okay not to try so hard.

44:49.896 --> 44:52.857
It's not okay, Grandma.

44:52.940 --> 44:55.776
I'm barely scraping by
in the fourth division.

44:56.402 --> 44:58.070
Sometimes life is like that.

44:59.113 --> 45:02.617
Things don't always go
the way you want them to.

45:04.493 --> 45:05.703
You're right.

45:07.246 --> 45:09.999
Life really doesn't go
the way you want it to.

45:10.875 --> 45:12.335
What's wrong now?

45:13.002 --> 45:17.089
In my original life and in this one,

45:18.633 --> 45:21.219
I can't seem to give you
the life you deserve.

45:22.261 --> 45:24.889
- Stop that.
- But it's true.

45:24.972 --> 45:27.183
When I had money, you weren't around.

45:27.725 --> 45:29.185
And looking at my life now,

45:29.685 --> 45:32.813
I probably haven't even been able
to take you on a trip abroad.

45:32.897 --> 45:36.984
I don't care about any of that.

45:38.152 --> 45:41.948
All the other grandmothers here
are actually envious of me.

45:43.491 --> 45:46.035
Why? What are they envious of?

45:47.036 --> 45:50.665
They're envious because my grandson
is so sweet and visits often.

45:50.748 --> 45:53.501
And besides, I tell them

45:53.584 --> 45:57.296
that my grandson has taken me
to every corner of the country.

45:57.380 --> 46:01.759
When I show them the pictures,
they get so jealous.

46:03.261 --> 46:06.389
I… did that?

46:06.472 --> 46:07.682
Of course.

46:08.266 --> 46:10.893
You took me to see the flowers
when they bloomed,

46:10.977 --> 46:14.397
to the water when it got hot,

46:14.480 --> 46:18.317
and to the mountains to see
the vibrant autumn leaves.

46:18.401 --> 46:20.027
Then, when it got cold,

46:21.028 --> 46:22.905
you took me to the hot springs.

46:23.990 --> 46:25.574
Here, look at this.

46:26.450 --> 46:29.453
This was when we went to Yeosu.

46:30.288 --> 46:31.539
MYEONGDONG DAK-GALBI ALLEY

46:31.622 --> 46:36.210
And this was when we went to Chuncheon
for some dak-galbi. Goodness.

46:36.294 --> 46:40.965
You wandered off,
and I looked everywhere for you.

46:41.048 --> 46:44.552
And this was when we went to Pocheon.

46:44.635 --> 46:49.140
You remember the prehistoric site
with the cavemen doing this?

46:49.223 --> 46:50.850
We did that together.

47:06.657 --> 47:09.493
He's a grown man.
Why was he crying like that?

47:09.577 --> 47:11.245
He startled me.

47:17.460 --> 47:18.878
Gosh, you scared me!

47:20.963 --> 47:23.299
- It's you, right?
- What?

47:23.799 --> 47:25.801
It is you.

47:26.344 --> 47:28.554
I know everything.

47:29.263 --> 47:31.766
I know this is all your fault!

47:31.849 --> 47:33.351
What?

47:36.228 --> 47:41.108
Die, die, die!

47:41.192 --> 47:42.526
Sir, what are you doing?

47:42.610 --> 47:43.986
Get off me!

48:11.097 --> 48:12.556
I am so sorry.

48:12.640 --> 48:14.892
I'm truly sorry.

48:14.975 --> 48:17.478
Are you all right?

48:18.437 --> 48:20.147
As you can see, I'm not dead.

48:20.231 --> 48:22.149
Though he nearly killed me.

48:22.233 --> 48:23.692
You must've been so scared.

48:23.776 --> 48:25.778
That's not the issue here.

48:25.861 --> 48:27.571
She could've been seriously hurt!

48:29.365 --> 48:31.325
I'm so sorry.

48:33.994 --> 48:36.122
But why did he attack her all of a sudden?

48:36.997 --> 48:38.624
That looks painful.

48:39.625 --> 48:40.918
Sir.

48:42.211 --> 48:43.963
Why on earth did you do that?

48:47.007 --> 48:48.134
What?

48:50.219 --> 48:53.055
Me? What did I do?

48:54.598 --> 48:55.766
Never mind.

48:56.517 --> 48:58.352
He's usually such a gentle man.

48:59.061 --> 49:03.482
Well, my father-in-law
isn't as stable as he used to be.

49:03.566 --> 49:06.819
He's been showing symptoms
of dementia for a few years.

49:06.902 --> 49:08.654
He doesn't even recognize us.

49:09.321 --> 49:10.614
I see.

49:10.698 --> 49:14.034
But nothing like this
has ever happened before.

49:14.535 --> 49:15.744
I'm so sorry.

49:17.872 --> 49:22.084
I'm Hwang Dong-sik's son.

49:23.002 --> 49:25.588
I'm sorry for being late.
I only just heard the news.

49:26.755 --> 49:28.299
Hwang Dong-sik?

49:28.382 --> 49:31.218
I'm very sorry about my father.

49:33.512 --> 49:35.222
Are you badly hurt?

49:36.557 --> 49:39.768
Your face looks so familiar.

49:44.523 --> 49:46.734
THIRTY YEARS AGO

49:57.244 --> 49:58.329
Hey.

50:05.044 --> 50:07.963
I think I remember now.

50:09.340 --> 50:11.800
You look just like
that old man did back then.

50:19.433 --> 50:21.101
Forget it. You can leave now.

50:21.852 --> 50:24.104
- Still--
- Didn't you come to apologize?

50:24.188 --> 50:26.315
You apologized, and I accepted it.

50:26.398 --> 50:27.399
So we're done.

50:28.150 --> 50:30.361
Si-yeol, I'm tired. Let's go home.

50:31.487 --> 50:32.905
Okay.

51:07.606 --> 51:08.857
Is she okay?

51:10.526 --> 51:12.778
Why is she in such a foul mood?

51:22.788 --> 51:23.706
KANG SI-YEOL'S ACCOUNT

51:23.789 --> 51:24.999
For crying out loud.

51:25.874 --> 51:29.587
I'm flat broke.
Is this really all I have left?

51:31.130 --> 51:34.675
I can barely survive a month with this.

51:45.269 --> 51:47.104
This is so frustrating.

52:07.916 --> 52:09.918
What's that smell?

52:22.723 --> 52:23.974
What are you doing?

52:24.767 --> 52:26.268
Oh, hey.

52:26.977 --> 52:28.729
Just wait a bit. It's almost ready.

52:38.614 --> 52:41.700
Why did you get pork shoulder?
I prefer pork belly.

52:41.784 --> 52:44.703
Just eat what you're given.

52:50.626 --> 52:52.878
What? Why is this so good?

52:53.504 --> 52:54.922
Is it good?

52:55.005 --> 52:58.550
It's been a while since I cooked,
so I wasn't sure about the taste.

52:59.385 --> 53:01.095
Not bad.

53:01.637 --> 53:05.557
Since you had money, I thought
you'd just have people cook for you.

53:07.017 --> 53:11.313
You really do have a knack
for backhanded compliments.

53:16.735 --> 53:20.948
You've been sighing since yesterday
about having no money.

53:21.031 --> 53:22.449
Why the sudden feast?

53:22.533 --> 53:25.452
Well, I've always wanted to try

53:26.120 --> 53:28.997
grilled meat with soju.

53:33.752 --> 53:35.421
Plus, you seemed a bit down.

53:36.046 --> 53:37.172
Me?

53:40.217 --> 53:41.301
That's right.

53:41.802 --> 53:43.053
Now that you mention it,

53:43.137 --> 53:46.265
I think my mood is actually pretty rotten.

53:46.348 --> 53:51.145
Is it related to the ones above again?

53:51.770 --> 53:52.813
Yes.

54:01.655 --> 54:04.616
Man, those guys.

54:05.117 --> 54:07.578
If they have something to say,
they should just say it clearly.

54:07.661 --> 54:10.998
Why are they always sending
such cryptic signals?

54:11.999 --> 54:13.083
Actually,

54:14.293 --> 54:16.420
the message was fairly clear this time.

54:17.838 --> 54:18.756
Really?

54:20.382 --> 54:21.467
What's the message?

54:22.134 --> 54:24.011
That I've lived my life wrong.

54:25.804 --> 54:29.808
I think that old man earlier
was a client of mine.

54:29.892 --> 54:30.893
His face looked familiar.

54:31.727 --> 54:32.603
A client?

54:32.686 --> 54:37.107
What did you do to him
to make him act like that toward you?

54:37.816 --> 54:40.903
Who knows? I've had plenty
of clients just pass through.

54:40.986 --> 54:43.530
It's not like I remember
every single one of their stories.

54:43.614 --> 54:47.201
But I'm sure he has a reason
to hold a grudge against me.

54:47.910 --> 54:48.994
I see.

54:50.370 --> 54:54.708
Having been through it myself,
I'm not exactly surprised.

54:56.877 --> 54:58.003
What?

54:58.545 --> 55:01.590
So, is that why you've been
feeling so low?

55:04.760 --> 55:06.136
When I first became human,

55:07.387 --> 55:11.308
I wondered why my reward
for good deeds was a life like this.

55:12.935 --> 55:16.939
But I guess this is
just their way of punishing me.

55:18.065 --> 55:20.901
They forced me to become human
when I never wanted to,

55:20.984 --> 55:23.654
shoved past misdeeds
I don't even remember right in my face,

55:23.737 --> 55:26.448
and now they probably want me
to reflect on them.

55:32.246 --> 55:34.081
I am sorry about all this.

55:34.790 --> 55:36.250
You're getting punished along with me,

55:36.333 --> 55:37.960
even though I caused this mess.

55:41.421 --> 55:42.631
I don't know about that.

55:43.590 --> 55:46.051
I don't see it that way at all.

55:49.596 --> 55:50.806
What?

55:50.889 --> 55:54.685
The anniversary of my grandma's death
was a few days ago.

55:55.727 --> 55:56.770
I see.

55:58.772 --> 55:59.857
You know,

56:00.440 --> 56:05.779
I always used to say
that I'd spoil her when I made it big.

56:07.656 --> 56:10.909
But she collapsed
during my first season in Europe.

56:15.205 --> 56:16.915
She was all alone,

56:16.999 --> 56:19.751
so by the time she was found,
she was already gone.

56:29.344 --> 56:32.848
When you made this switch happen,

56:34.641 --> 56:38.061
I thought that everything
that was precious and important to me

56:39.187 --> 56:41.523
had vanished.

56:43.984 --> 56:45.110
I was wrong, though.

56:47.738 --> 56:49.197
What I'm saying is…

56:51.283 --> 56:54.286
you don't have to feel so sorry for me.

56:54.828 --> 56:56.872
I don't feel like I'm being punished.

57:03.003 --> 57:05.339
We're going to go back
to the way things were anyway.

57:06.173 --> 57:10.427
So once all of this is over and behind us,

57:11.053 --> 57:14.765
I think I'll remember this moment
like a special dream.

57:15.724 --> 57:17.476
When I think of it like that,

57:17.559 --> 57:20.437
even the bad or uncomfortable parts

57:22.397 --> 57:24.441
feel like a unique vacation.

57:27.653 --> 57:29.071
"A special dream"?

57:29.947 --> 57:31.406
More like a nightmare.

57:34.618 --> 57:35.744
What about you?

57:36.662 --> 57:40.207
Was there really nothing good
about becoming human?

57:42.209 --> 57:43.085
What?

57:44.711 --> 57:45.837
Nothing at all?

57:56.223 --> 57:58.642
No, there is something.

58:00.352 --> 58:02.104
That's a relief.

58:03.105 --> 58:04.022
What is it?

58:07.985 --> 58:09.027
You.

58:18.370 --> 58:19.705
Maybe it's because I'm human now,

58:19.788 --> 58:22.708
but my heart keeps racing
for no reason whenever I look at you.

58:24.042 --> 58:27.295
I guess this is
what humans call romantic feelings.

58:29.631 --> 58:30.507
What?

58:31.883 --> 58:36.096
Si-yeol, I think I need to date you.

59:01.955 --> 59:03.915
SPECIAL APPEARANCES
BY JUNG DONG-HWAN AND OH MIN-SEOK

59:28.065 --> 59:30.984
NO TAIL TO TELL

59:31.068 --> 59:33.028
- Open wide.
- What are you doing?

59:33.111 --> 59:34.738
How about a date today?

59:35.280 --> 59:37.574
I think I finally know what we have to do.

59:37.657 --> 59:38.992
Do you want to win?

59:39.076 --> 59:41.495
I'll make sure you move up
to the third division.

59:44.623 --> 59:46.458
- Dad!
- How about it?

59:47.709 --> 59:48.877
Do you remember now?

59:49.669 --> 59:51.963
Where is the chairman right now?

59:53.006 --> 59:56.343
So, fixing the misdeeds
you committed in the past

59:56.426 --> 59:57.469
is the will of Heaven?

59:58.637 --> 01:00:02.057
Does it look like I'm here to negotiate?

01:00:04.534 --> 01:00:06.534
Subtitle translation by Susanna Kim
